            <ArticleTitle>A comparison of diclofenac with and without single-dose intravenous steroid to prevent postoperative pain after third molar removal.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>634-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The efficacy of 40 mg of methylprednisolone given intravenously before operation in combination with orally administered rapid-release and sustained-release diclofenac preparations in preventing postoperative pain after third molar removal was studied. The administration of methylprednisolone and diclofenac resulted in greater pain relief than did administration of diclofenac alone.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
